#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Configuring-QoS-Overrides.rst:12
msgid ""
"Quality of Service (QoS) overrides allow configuring publisher and "
"subscription QoS profiles at node startup without modifying application "
"source code. This tutorial demonstrates how to enable QoS overrides in C++ "
"and Python nodes and configure them using parameter files. After following "
"these steps, you will be able to inspect, configure, and validate QoS "
"policies at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Configuring-QoS-Overrides.rst:20
msgid ""
"**Goal:** Enable and configure Quality of Service (QoS) overrides for "
"publishers and subscriptions using ROS 2 parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Configuring-QoS-Overrides.rst:22
msgid "**Tutorial level:** Intermediate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Configuring-QoS-Overrides.rst:24
msgid "**Time:** 15 minutes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Configuring-QoS-Overrides.rst:28
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Configuring-QoS-Overrides.rst:31
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Configuring-QoS-Overrides.rst:33
msgid ""
"In ROS 2, Quality of Service (QoS) profiles determine the frequency, "
"reliability, and overall performance of communication between publishers and "
"subscribers on a ROS topic. By default, developers specify QoS settings "
"directly in their application source code when creating publishers and "
"subscriptions. However, hard-coded QoS settings make it difficult to adapt "
"nodes to different deployment environments. For example, a robot might use "
"reliable communications over a wired gigabit network during development, but "
"require best-effort communications over a lossy wireless connection in "
"deployment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Configuring-QoS-Overrides.rst:38
msgid ""
"To address this challenge, ROS 2 provides **QoS overrides**. QoS overrides "
"allow developers to expose publisher and subscription QoS configurations as "
"read-only ROS 2 parameters under a hierarchical parameter prefix "
"(``qos_overrides.<topic>...``). Users can then change QoS policies at node "
"startup using YAML parameter files or command-line arguments without "
"recompiling or altering the node source code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Configuring-QoS-Overrides.rst:43
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

